\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Brazil Real Gains Against Dollar on U.S. Budget, Debt Debates\b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2013\par 21:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real strengthened against the dollar in Monday trading as concern grew that the \uc2 U.S. Congress\uc2  would fail to avoid a partial government shutdown ahead of a debate over raising the country's debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.2145 to the dollar, stronger than the Friday close of BRL2.2555, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 U.S. lawmakers on Monday raced to settle on a budget deal with the government seemingly headed for a partial shutdown for the first time since 1996. That comes ahead of another battle the Congress will face in coming weeks, when it debates raising the debt ceiling before a mid-October deadline.\par \par \uc2 The uncertainty led the dollar lower against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the real being no exception. Adding to the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength on Monday was the approaching expiration of futures contracts. Monthly \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures contracts expire Tuesday. They will close out based on Monday's average \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, or Ptax rate. Expiry of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures contracts typically brings high volume to Brazil's spot market as holders of short-dollar positions battle with holders of long positions to influence the Ptax rate.\par \par \uc2 "It's all about the futures expiry," said Vanderlei Muniz, partner in southern Brazil's Onnix brokerage. "Holders of long positions are fighting it out with holders of short positions."\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is continuing its policy of daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an effort to maintain orderly trading. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been auctioning the equivalent of about $500 million in daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts, which allow investors to exchange bonds linked to domestic interest rates for paper indexed directly to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 --Tom Murphy in Sao Paulo contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paulo Winterstein at paulo.winterstein@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 30, 2013 15:42 ET (19:42 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130930e99u004ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
