\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Tombini:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Markets To Continue\b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2013\par 17:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 24 Sep 2013 11:51 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Tombini: Reversal Of Fed Policies Delayed, Not Canceled\par \par \uc2 24 Sep 2013 11:51 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Tombini: \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  To Keep Program To Curb Volatility\par \par \uc2 24 Sep 2013 11:51 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Tombini Talks To Senators About Monetary Policy\par \par \uc2 24 Sep 2013 12:13 EDT DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Tombini: \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Markets to Continue\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Paulo Trevisani \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BRASILIA--\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will keep its actions on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets as planned to help the economy transition to when the U.S. stops flooding markets with dollars.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. Federal Reserve "has just postponed" the reversal of its easy-money policy, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazil \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Alexandre Tombini said during Senate testimony Tuesday. The reversal "will happen sometime in the future," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the real, has been very much influenced by Fed policies in the past few years.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fed actions aimed at jump-starting the U.S. economy caused larger-than-usual availability of dollars in global market. That made the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lose value against the real and made Brazilian exports less competitive.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But signs that the Fed was about to bring the easy-money policy to an end sent the real into a tailspin in the last few months, forcing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to start a program of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to put a floor under the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Tombini said the program will remain in place, even after the Fed's decision last week to keep in place the bond-buying program that has injected dollars in global markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to act to reduce volatility," Mr. Tombini said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Paulo Trevisani at paulo.trevisani@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 24, 2013 12:13 ET (16:13 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130924e99o003rb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
