\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Strengthens For Second Day On Fed Reprieve\b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2013\par 14:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--Brazil's real strengthened against the dollar again in early Thursday trading after the Federal Reserve said it would continue with its bond-buying program, easing concern there would be fewer dollars available on the market.\par \par \uc2 The real was trading at 2.1872 to the dollar at the open of regular trading, after ending at BRL2.1993 to the dollar Wednesday, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Following a meeting of the Fed's open market committee, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it planned to wait a while longer before curtailing its $85 billion-a-month bond-buying program so it can further evaluate the effect of the stimulus.\par \par \uc2 "The Fed's decision yesterday not to taper its asset purchases just yet provides some breathing room for the more troubled emerging economies," Capital Economics wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 With the expectation in recent weeks that the Fed would wind down its program, the real fell drastically against the dollar, trading as weak as BRL2.45 per dollar. Following persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, the real was able to recoup part of its losses, and stabilized at around BRL2.25 per dollar. With Wednesday's announcement, the real strengthened past BRL2.20 per dollar for the first time since June.\par \par \uc2 But Capital Economics warned that "yesterday's decision by the Fed is best viewed as a temporary reprieve rather than a stay of execution," and emerging markets such as Brazil need to get their house in order to avoid wild swings in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the future.\par \par \uc2 Brazil must get its fiscal policy in order and bolster government finances, as well as address "growing financial vulnerabilities resulting from a recent credit binge," Capital Economics wrote.\par \par \uc2 -Write to Paulo Winterstein at paulo.winterstein@wsj.com [ 19-09-13 1222GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130919e99j000fs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
