\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Loses Momentum, Closes Slightly Weaker\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2013\par 22:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO--Brazil's real changed course and closed slightly weaker against the dollar Monday, as enthusiasm about Lawrence Summers's exit from the contest to lead the U.S. Federal Reserve faded and investors' attention drifted back to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lackluster fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.2767 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, compared with BRL2.2751 at Friday's close.\par \par \uc2 The real had strengthened sharply in first hour or so of trading on news that Mr. Summers, believed to favor an earlier end to the monetary stimulus programs that propped up the real and other assets in recent years, left the running to become the next Fed chairman.\par \par \uc2 But with speculators sitting mostly on the sidelines in the weeks since \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  implemented routine, daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local futures market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost momentum over the course of the session. Traders say volume has been low.\par \par \uc2 "I think the exchange rate is just reflecting fundamentals right now, since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to neutralize the speculative part of the market," said Sidnei Nehme, director of Sao Paulo's NGO trading house.\par \par \uc2 After a rise in volatility during July and August that saw the real weaken to a four-year low of about BRL2.45 to the dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has consolidated in the BRL2.25-BRL2.30 range in the past week or so. Mr. Nehme said he thinks it will stay there, at least until Brazil starts drawing capital back into the country.\par \par \uc2 Sluggish growth, high inflation and questionable economic policy-making have undermined Brazil's credentials as a promising emerging market in the eyes of investors. At the same time, prices for the main commodities that Brazil exports have settled below the highs of 2011 and 2012.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paul Kiernan at paul.kiernan@dowjones.com [ 16-09-13 2027GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130916e99g000ja\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
