\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Dollar Falls Against Most Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 599 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2013\par 18:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar weakened against most emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday on the expectation that the current policy would continue at the Federal Reserve under the next chairman.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, Larry Summers stepped down as a potential candidate to replace current Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke. Many believe that Janet Yellen, the Fed's current vice chairwoman, and Donald Kohn, the Fed's past vice chairman, are likely top contenders for the post. There are expectations that whoever succeeds Mr. Bernanke will continue the present course of monetary policy in the U.S. for the next few years and that any scaling back of the Fed's aggressive steps to stimulate the economy will be gradual.\par \par \uc2 This ended some uncertainty about future policy and led to a sharp market rally which saw many emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  notch gains exceeding 1% to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "It's a case of dollar weakness not emerging-market strength," said Peter Kinsella, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 He cautions that much of the structural problems in these developing nations, such as wide current account deficits and slowing growth, continue to dominate their outlook, despite some improved data in recent weeks from China and Brazil.\par \par \uc2 Also, investors are hesitant to make any bets ahead of the critical Fed meeting this week, at which policy makers will debate whether to start scaling back bond purchases. There are prevalent expectations in the markets that the Fed could announce tapering Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "This rally is a flash in the pan," he said, adding that "buying into emerging markets is a bit premature."\par \par \uc2 If the Fed scales back bond buying, the flow of money into emerging nations is expected to drop, leading to a sharp fall in demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bonds and stocks of these countries.\par \par \uc2 The dollar, which fell against the Turkish lira, was trading below TRY2 for the first time since August. Currently, the pair trades at TRY1.9938, 1.75% weaker on the day, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market during the day to further support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, the bank is expected to hold rates steady at its rate-setting meeting Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 South Africa also saw its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  benefit from the lift in sentiment. The dollar weakened 1.25% to the rand to trade at ZAR9.8078, according to CQG data. The rand's clear break from the ZAR10 to the dollar levels suggest that \uc2 South Africa's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't change its policy rate on Thursday, wrote analysts at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While the dollar continues to remain weaker to the Brazilian real on the day, it has recouped much of its losses from earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 The dollar currently fetches BRL2.2732 from its earlier low of BRL2.2482, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 The retrenchment was despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a survey that raised \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's growth rate to 2.4% this year.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the equivalent of $1.96 billion in foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts Monday in an auction to roll over several blocks of contracts that are maturing. The sale of dollars, typically, is supportive of the real.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey found that economists now project Brazil's economy will improve in the coming quarters on improved industrial production. Still, expectations of higher inflation and poor policy continue to disappoint investors.\par \par \uc2 Write to Prabha Natarajan at prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 16, 2013 12:39 ET (16:39 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130916e99g003vk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
