\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Emerging nations to fight alone against further  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  falls\b0\par\par\uc2 By Silvio Cascione and Rahul Karunakar   \par \uc2 728 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2013\par 12:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/BANGALORE, Sept 5 (Reuters) - Emerging nations are unlikely to join forces to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in the next few weeks to prop up their ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even though there is more pain ahead, a Reuters poll predicted.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve's move toward trimming its stimulus has triggered a sell-off in emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a flight to the dollar, resulting in a round of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and monetary policy moves from Istanbul to Mumbai to prop them up.\par \par \uc2 The survey of over 50 leading \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists showed deep skepticism about India's plans to seek support for coordinated offshore \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with analysts saying each developing country will fight their own battle against further falls.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, the probability of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by emerging-nation central banks within the next few weeks is just 15 percent, according to the poll consensus. Only three institutions said the likelihood is greater than 50 percent.\par \par \uc2 "I see India is suffering a lot, but this affects other nations in very different ways, and each one of them has different needs. I'm very skeptical about joint action," said Newton Rosa, chief economist at SulAm\u233\'00\'E9rica Investimentos, a Brazilian asset management firm owned by Dutch bank \uc2 ING Group\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Reuters poll results come as leaders and policymakers from the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  developed and emerging nations meet this week in St. Petersburg, Russia, with the effects on the global economy from the Fed's pull-back high on the agenda.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reported exclusively last month that India was seeking support from fellow emerging market countries for coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but had received little public backing from other nations.\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee has lost nearly 20 percent to the dollar this year, hitting record lows almost daily since end of May, when Fed Chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2  hinted at a stimulus rollback.\par \par \uc2 However, the need for urgent action seems to be lower in Brazil than in India.\par \par \uc2 After a near 20-percent plunge in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from May to mid-August, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  has announced a huge \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program with up to $60 billion in derivatives and repurchase agreements by year-end, and has been successful so far in stabilizing the real.\par \par \uc2 "Each country has it own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy. For example, India and Argentina adopted capital controls, while Brazil offered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps," said Adriano Beuren, an economist with Banco Sicredi, in Porto Alegre, Brazil.\par \par \uc2 "The need for foreign money is different in each country. That creates difficulties for a deal."\par \par \uc2 Economists in Brazil were particularly skeptical of such a move following comments by Finance Minister Guido Mantega that the largest Latin American country, one of the most affected by the emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rout, was not involved in any plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in offshore \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 What has kept leading emerging countries busy, Mantega said, are plans to create a bank and a reserve fund by the BRICS group - including Brazil, Russia, India, China and South Africa.\par \par \uc2 China's deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, \uc2 Yi Gang\uc2 , also called on Wednesday for China and other Asian countries to broaden the use of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in bilateral trade and investment settlements and close more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap deals to facilitate capital flows.\par \par \uc2 The Fed is expected to start reducing its $85 billion per month bond-buying programme when it meets on September 17-18, according to all nine of the Reuters polls of economists conducted on the subject.\par \par \uc2 If the Fed goes ahead with its plan then emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected to trade lower, according to 30 of 53 analysts polled. Another 13 said significantly lower, three said unchanged while the remaining seven said somewhat higher.\par \par \uc2 "There is probably still more downside for the emerging markets but they've been hit pretty hard already so there may not be that much more downside," said Benjamin Reitzes, a senior economist at BMO Capital Markets.\par \par \uc2 The global Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll this week found the U.S. dollar is the only \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that stands to benefit in the near-term from that. (Additional polling by Shaloo Shrivastava in Bangalore; Editing by Toby Chopra)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -POLL/BRICS (POLL) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | AFN | BRS | G | RBN | SF | SNI | SNS | UKI | Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130905e995000hm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pi