\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Ends Stronger on Local Rate View\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 438 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2013\par 22:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--Brazil's real gained ground against the dollar to end stronger Thursday after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reinforced hints that it would continue to raise local interest rates through the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 The real exited regular trading at BRL2.3202 to the dollar after ending at BRL2.3542 to the dollar Wednesday, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversed early weakening to make a sharp move stronger midway through the session. The real's move stronger came as the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pledged to hold firm against the inflationary effects of recent depreciation in the minutes of its August rate meeting.\par \par \uc2 "Following today's minutes, we revise our Selic forecasts and now expect interest rates to be adjusted by 50bps and 25bps in October and November, respectively," said Enestor dos Santos, analyst at \uc2 BBVA\uc2 . "This is broadly driven by the recent depreciation of the exchange rate."\par \par \uc2 In the minutes, the bank raised its reference rate for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to BRL2.40 to the dollar from BRL2.25 previously, and acknowledged a negative impact for inflation.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the influence of the minutes seemed to overshadow the effect of upbeat economic news in the U.S., where improvements in jobs data and service-sector activity reinforced the possibility of monetary-policy tightening there as well.\par \par \uc2 The prospect of rising rates in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  also dovetailed with the growing impact of exchange market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $497.3 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps early in the session Thursday as part of its ongoing effort to provide liquidity and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedge to the market.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has scheduled some $100 billion in swap and dollar repurchase auctions for the end of the year. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps allow investors to exchange bonds indexed to domestic interest rates for paper tied directly to the U.S. dollar and frequently lead to a strengthening of the Brazilian real.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted that with the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , investors were backing away from recent projections of a stronger long term weakening of the real.\par \par \uc2 "The sudden strengthening of the real was a clear sign that investors are unwinding some long dollar positions," said Reginaldo Galhardo, \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Manager at the Treviso brokerage.\par \par \uc2 The trend was reinforced earlier in the week when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  over a two day period sold some $2.5 billion in swaps above the amount of its scheduled daily auctions.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 05-09-13 2001GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130905e995000o9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
