\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Opens Stronger As  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\uc2  Continues\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paulo Winterstein   \par \uc2 606 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2013\par 15:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real strengthened slightly on Wednesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , offsetting the global search for dollars as the situation in the Middle East continues to worry investors.\par \par \uc2 The real was trading at BRL2.3541 to the dollar, somewhat stronger than Tuesday's close of BRL2.3576 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Investors are starting to gain confidence in the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to ease volatility in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan launched last month. The bank is offering \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts worth $500 million a day and will sell up to $1 billion each Friday with an agreement to repurchase the dollars at a later date.\par \par \uc2 That \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped ease concern that the real would weaken significantly, sending investors and companies that need to pay dollar-denominated costs scrambling for cover. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to announce \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows in the middle of the day, which could show a continued deterioration. During the first 23 days of August, more than $2.7 billion left the country, reducing the inflow of dollars so far this year to $5.3 billion.\par \par \uc2 Concern about flows has become more of an issue as the U.S. considers military action in Syria. President Barack Obama has asked \uc2 U.S. Congress\uc2  to approve military action, and as a result many traders are taking investments out of emerging markets to park their investments in dollars, seen as a secure harbor.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paulo Winterstein at paulo.winterstein@dowjones.com [ 04-09-13 1327GMT ]\par \par \uc2 By Paulo Winterstein\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--Brazil's real strengthened slightly against the dollar on Wednesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, helping offset the global search for dollars as the situation in the Middle East continues to worry investors.\par \par \uc2 The real exited from active trading at BRL2.3542 to the dollar, somewhat stronger than Tuesday's close of BRL2.3576 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Investors are starting to gain confidence in the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to ease volatility in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan launched last month. On Wednesday, the bank sold $498 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, part of its plan to offer swap contracts worth $500 million a day, alongside auctions to sell up to $1 billion each Friday with an agreement to repurchase the dollars at a later date.\par \par \uc2 Both contracts allow companies to hedge any dollar-denominated obligations against future volatility, and end up alleviating short-term demand for dollars by ensuring that a sufficient amount will be available later at an already-established price.\par \par \uc2 As a result, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped ease concern that the real would weaken significantly, even after it announced the continued exit of dollars from Brazil. During the month of August, Brazil saw a net outflow of $5.85 billion dollars, reducing the net inflow for the first eight months of 2013 to $2.24 billion. That compares with an inflow of almost $23 billion during the year-earlier period.\par \par \uc2 Concern about flows has become more of an issue as the U.S. considers military action in Syria. President Barack Obama has asked the \uc2 U.S. Congress\uc2  to approve military action, and as a result many traders are taking investments out of emerging markets to park their investments in dollars, seen as a secure harbor.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paulo Winterstein at paulo.winterstein@dowjones.com [ 04-09-13 1950GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130904e994000g9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
