\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  up on China data, but sentiment fragile\b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2013\par 20:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Sept 4 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed on Wednesday as strong Chinese service sector data supported investors' appetite for risk, although sentiment remained fragile with a possible strike in Syria and prospects for less U.S. stimulus. The Mexican peso gained 0.5 percent after data showed China's services sector hit a five-month high in August, the latest evidence that the largest consumer of Latin American commodities may have avoided a sharp slowdown. The Brazilian real edged 0.1 percent higher, also supported by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sale of 10,000 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, derivatives that give investors protection against losses in the real. The swap sale was part of a $60 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program announced by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month. The plan is expected to stabilize the real at around 2.35 per dollar over the next few months, according to a Reuters survey of 33 banks and research firms.\par \par \uc2  Risks to the performance of emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained high, however, as President Barack Obama continued to push for congressional approval to launch a limited military strike on Syria. Fears that the U.S. Federal Reserve may this month announce a pullback in its bond-buying program also kept investors on edge. The Fed's program has provided a steady source of dollars seeking higher returns in emerging markets over the past few years. "The market remains more fearful than cheerful. Everybody is trying to limit losses," said Reginaldo Galhardo, a manager at the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  desk of Treviso brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par        \par     Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prices at 1744 GMT:\par     \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                         daily %    YTD %\par                                     change   change\par                            Latest           \par  Brazil real               2.3561     0.13   -13.42\par                                             \par  Mexico peso              13.3250     0.53    -3.46\par                                             \par  Chile peso              509.0000     0.20    -5.95\par                                             \par  Colombia peso          1940.2600     0.27    -8.98\par                                             \par  Peru sol                  2.8070     0.04    -9.12\par                                             \par  Argentina peso            5.7000    -0.13   -13.82\par  (interbank)                                \par                                             \par  Argentina peso            9.2100     0.43   -26.38\par  (parallel)                                 \par                                             \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Marilia Carrera and Walter Brandimarte; editing by Andrew Hay)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  | ABN | D | M | RBN | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130907e99400095\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
