\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Brazil has 'ammunition' to combat global turmoil, Rousseff says\b0\par\par\uc2 465 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 2013\par 15:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Aug 28 (Reuters) - The Brazilian economy has enough firepower to stem the impact of global market turmoil, President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2  said on Wednesday, in an attempt to reinforce confidence in the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rousseff blamed the recent slump in the real, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , on expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve is on its way to tightening monetary policy. She said Brazil has "large international reserves," which she suggested were "ammunition" that could help ease market volatility.\par \par \uc2 "Do you know that old story about keeping your money beneath your mattress? Well, Brazil doesn't but it does have between $378 billion and $372 billion in international reserves," she told radio stations in the city of Belo Horizonte in an interview. "We have what is called 'ammunition' to deal with those global situations."\par \par \uc2 Investors are questioning Rousseff's economic policy, saying it has made the country more vulnerable to rising debt and inflation, state interference in some sectors and a weaker real. The government has defended its stance by saying policies - such as ample tax breaks and loan disbursements from state-run banks to aid the industry - are cushioning Brazil from global turmoil.\par \par \uc2 WHIPLASH\par \par \uc2 The real, along with India's rupee, has weakened more than any other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since May. Its tumble of over 15 percent is forcing businesses, policymakers and consumers to prepare for consequences, including inflation and a costlier fundraising.\par \par \uc2 The decline has become another symbol of Brazil's fall from grace among investors and produced a severe case of whiplash among producers, who complain that the basic pillars of Latin America's largest economy have constantly shifted under Rousseff's left-leaning government.\par \par \uc2 Rousseff reiterated that the government is neither targeting any level nor a direction for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "Our policy is one of a flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she said in the interview.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened 0.6 percent to 2.358 to the dollar in late morning trading, running counter to global markets.\par \par \uc2 In an effort to shore up the real and stem volatility, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Thursday said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets with daily cash and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps valued at $60 billion by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy committee, known as Copom, is widely expected to deliver another half a percentage point hike in interest rates on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's low growth in her 2 1/2-year tenure as president has been the result of a slow global expansion, Rousseff said, adding that Brazil's public finances remain "very good."\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-ECONOMY/ROUSSEFF (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | C | O | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130828e98s000n2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
