\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Brazil's Government Will Not Allow Excessive  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Volatility -Mantega\b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2013\par 20:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 26 Aug 2013 14:14 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Could \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Spot Market, If Needed -Mantega\par \par \uc2 26 Aug 2013 14:15 EDT *DJ  Turbulence in Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market Coming Mainly From Overseas -Mantega\par \par \uc2 26 Aug 2013 14:29 EDT DJ  Brazil's Government Will Not Allow Excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Volatility - Mantega\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--Brazil's government will not allow excessive volatility in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and reserves the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever necessary to curb abrupt shifts in the value of the Brazilian real, Finance Minister Guido Mantega said Monday.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a news conference, the minister said, "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not allow excessive fluctuations in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  values."\par \par \uc2 He noted that the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent weeks, mainly via the sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts on the futures market and through auctions of short-term U.S. dollar credit lines.\par \par \uc2 However, he added, "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in spot trading, if necessary."\par \par \uc2 So far, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has avoided the direct sale of U.S. dollars from its foreign reserves. Reserves stand at over $370 billion.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real has seen a 14% depreciation against the U.S. dollar so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Mantega said, "Most of the pressure has come from the futures market, not the spot market." Consequently, the government has preferred to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in futures trading, through the swap contract auctions, rather than the spot market.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Mantega added, "Most of the volatility is coming from overseas, not from us." He said volatility struck the Brazilian market when the U.S. Federal Reserve Board began hinting that it would gradually reduce U.S. dollar liquidity in world markets. The expected policy shift has led to higher U.S. interest rates, which tend to siphon investment money away from emerging-market countries such as Brazil and back to the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Write to Rogerio Jelmayer at rogerio.jelmayer@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 26, 2013 14:29 ET (18:29 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130826e98q003ow\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
