\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Real soars on cenbank plan, U.S. data buoys Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2013\par 23:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte SAO PAULO, Aug 23 (Reuters) - Brazil's real rallied more than 3 percent on Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unveiled a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program that will provide $60 billion worth of cash and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedges to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the year-end. Weak U.S. housing data also supported the real and Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in general because it dented expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve will slow its monetary stimulus program next month. For years, bond buying by the Fed has provided a steady source of dollars seeking higher returns in emerging markets. Fears the bank would soon start cutting back on bond purchases have roiled most emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the Brazilian real was sold off more sharply than its peers because investors were also worried about the country's economic outlook.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan, announced after markets closed on Thursday, was seen by analysts as a bold move by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to give credibility to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. The bank failed to stop the real from slumping to near five-year lows over the past few days. The measure is likely to curb the recent extreme volatility of Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, allowing the real to trade more in line with peer \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Still, analysts say it is unlikely to reverse the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's depreciation, which is related to a global portfolio reallocation caused by the expected withdrawal of U.S. stimulus measures. "The measure should help contain excessive bearishness around the real and even bring it back to the 2.35-2.40 range," \uc2 Barclays\uc2  strategists Marcelo Salomon and Guilherme Loureiro wrote in a research note. The real closed at 2.3527 per dollar, 3.3 percent stronger for the day, while the Mexican peso gained 1 percent and the Chilean peso rose 0.4 percent. Brazilian interest rate futures <0#2DIJ:> also dropped sharply, with the contract maturing in January 2017 falling 43 basis points to 11.44 percent, as the outlook for a more stable real over the next few months eased concerns about inflation stemming from more expensive imported goods. Under its new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will sell, on Mondays through Thursdays, $500 million a day of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps - derivative contracts designed to provide investors with hedge against a weaker real. On Fridays, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will offer $1 billion on the spot market through repurchase agreements. The program "represents one of the boldest attempts yet by an emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the rout of recent weeks," Neil Shearing, chief emerging markets economist with Capital Economics in London, wrote in a note to clients. "It's worth noting that history suggests \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tends to smooth \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  adjustment, rather than prevent the adjustment from happening altogether," he added. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prices at 2100 GMT:\par        \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                          daily %    YTD %\par                                      change   change\par                             Latest           \par  Brazil real                2.3527     3.31   -13.29\par                                              \par  Mexico peso               12.9525     1.06    -0.68\par                                              \par  Chile peso               510.1000     0.37    -6.16\par                                              \par  Colombia peso           1916.7000    -0.04    -7.86\par                                              \par  Peru sol                   2.8110    -0.04    -9.25\par                                              \par  Argentina peso             5.6225    -0.13   -12.63\par  (interbank)                                 \par                                              \par  Argentina peso             9.1500     0.00   -25.90\par  (parallel)                                  \par                                              \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Tiago Pariz. Editing by Andre Grenon)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  | ABN | D | M | RBN | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130826e98n000xx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
