\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Gains Sharply After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Steps Up  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Matthew Cowley   \par \uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2013\par 14:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real gained sharply against the dollar on Friday morning, as a $60 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program unveiled by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  provided some much-needed relief to the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's program is aimed at providing companies and investors with the certainty they will be able to buy dollars if needed. It continues the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps taken by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days and weeks to try to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but adds more visibility and predictability.\par \par \uc2 "The measure should help contain excessive bearishness around the real and even bring it back to the 2.35-2.40 range," \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  said in a note. "But the measure should not reverse the weakening trend of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been driven by changes in U.S. monetary policy stance and uncertainty around local fiscal policy."\par \par \uc2 On Friday morning, the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained to BRL2.3811 per dollar, from BRL2.4406 late Thursday, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 Late Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would provide at least $60 billion more in dollar liquidity through the end of the year. Under the plan, the bank will offer $3 billion of dollar loans and swaps per week in daily auctions starting Friday through Dec. 31.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move was welcomed for providing more visibility to its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , replacing what have so far been unpredictable daily auctions. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already sold some $45 billion in dollar swap contracts so far this year. It is seen as continuing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of trying to restrain wild swings in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rather than halting it in its tracks.\par \par \uc2 "Crucially, [it] doesn't look like the government are trying to impact the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  too hard," said a London-based trader in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Unlike other central banks around the world, the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't have a direct impact on the country's $375 billion of foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 Yet the plan underscores how much the financial world has changed since the U.S. Federal Reserve said it was contemplating an end to the easy-money policies adopted to cope with the financial and economic crisis that began in 2008.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian officials in recent years have struggled with an overvalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not a falling one. Finance Minister Guido Mantega became known for complaining he was the victim of a "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war" as Brazil's real gained against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 That has now turned sharply. The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened around 16% against the dollar so far this year, and about 2% so far this week. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had touched BRL1.55 per dollar in mid-2011.\par \par \uc2 While much of the turn in market sentiment has been blamed on the Fed, the problems have been compounded by sluggish growth and high inflation in Brazil. Critics blame missteps in economic policy, including too much public spending, and say the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to weaken unless that changes.\par \par \uc2 "We reckon that the absence of any hint of a structural change in the economic policy mix is likely to limit the efficiency of such [\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] measures in the medium term," said Jankiel Santos, chief economist at BES Investimentos in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Write to \uc2 Matthew Cowley\uc2  at matthew.cowley@wsj.com [ 08-23-13 0849ET ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020130823e98n0001w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
