\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Plan Brings Relief To Emerging Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chiara Albanese   \par \uc2 932 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2013\par 13:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Measures announced by \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the real provided relief to a range of other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday, at the end of a turbulent week of losses unleashed by the prospect of tighter U.S. monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday it would provide at least $60 billion more in dollar liquidity through the end of the year, in an effort to limit the depreciation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one of the weakest links within the emerging markets space.\par \par \uc2 The news helped lift the real from a four-year low of BRL2.4560 to settle around BRL2.4350 in European hours before the local Brazilian market opens at 1200 GMT. Analysts said the move by Brazil was also helping other bruised emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the Turkish lira, to gain a more solid footing.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a positive sign for all emerging markets. It signalled investors that central banks are there and becoming more reactive and aggressive. They are ready to accelerate their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilize markets," said Luis Costa, an emerging market strategist at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sebastian Brown, an analyst at \uc2 Barclays\uc2 , said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could signal that "the tolerance for weaker exchange rates across emerging markets is close to running out, given some evidence of increasing inflationary pressures."\par \par \uc2 Countries with significant current account deficits have so far paid the highest price, reflecting investors' concerns that they will struggle to pull in the cash they need when the Federal Reserve starts winding down the easy-money era. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to taper it monthly $85 billion bond-buying program as early as September.\par \par \uc2 First in the firing line, and under significant strain earlier this week, are Indonesia, Turkey and India.\par \par \uc2 Since the end of May, both the rupee and the rupiah have lost about 15% against the U.S. dollar. The lira swooned to record lows Thursday. But after large declines this week, all have steadied Friday.\par \par \uc2 Also helping: Indonesian authorities on Friday announced a package of measures to stabilize the rupiah and to reduce the current account deficit, which will include the introduction of a higher import tax on luxury goods and the reduction of a quota on mineral exports.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Turkish lira has recovered somewhat. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  there launched an auction of $350 million for the second straight day.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's action will resonate with peers in \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Tim Ash, an analyst at Standard Bank in London. But like many other observers, Mr. Ash said the effect may prove fleeting. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program should provide a bit of short-term relief, but I'm not sure if it really will avoid the need in Turkey itself for a more substantive rise in policy rates. It could though buy them a bit more time," he said.\par \par \uc2 Some investors and analysts cautioned that beefed-up efforts to support hobbled \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are unlikely to end the pain.\par \par \uc2 "Measures provided some relief but the process of adjustment started at the end of May [when the Fed first hinted at a change in its monetary policy] has not finished yet. The dollar will continue to be firm. Treasury yields are not at equilibrium level and we expect more weakness of the emerging market side," said Clive Dennis, portfolio manager at Schroders, which had $388 billion under management at the end of June.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Costa at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  said the new measures in Brazil and Indonesia and persistent efforts by Turkey to ease the pressure on the lira are somewhat late. "The market has already deteriorated significantly since May. Will they be enough? Not yet. Central banks are under significant pressure to trigger growth in their economies," Mr. Costa added.\par \par \uc2 At 1040GMT, the euro was trading at $1.3363 against the dollar, compared with $1.3357 late Thursday in New York, according to trading system EBS.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was at Y98.938 against the yen, compared with Y98.72, while the euro was at Y32.20 compared with Y131.85.\par \par \uc2 The pound was trading at $1.5619 against the dollar, compared with $1.5586 late Thursday in New York. The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which tracks the dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was trading at 73.964, compared with 73.92 late Thursday in New York.\par \par \uc2 (Francis Bray contributed to the article)\par \par \uc2 Rolling 24-hour chart levels:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/USD    USD/JPY    GBP/USD    USD/CHF \par  \par Spot 1043 GMT     1.3363     98.93      1.5617     0.9243 \par 3 Day Trend       Bearish    Bullish    Bearish    Bearish \par Weekly Trend      Bullish    Range      Bullish    Bearish \par 200 day ma        1.3104     94.36      1.5476     0.9372 \par 3rd Resistance    1.3453     99.95      1.5715     0.9340 \par 2nd Resistance    1.3415     99.76      1.5680     0.9290 \par 1st Resistance    1.3386     99.14      1.5639     0.9268 \par Pivot*            1.3343     98.38      1.5593     0.9247 \par 1st Support       1.3335     98.66      1.5562     0.9225 \par 2nd Support       1.3298     98.33      1.5500     0.9200 \par 3rd Support       1.3260     97.95      1.5475     0.9180 \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/JPY \par  \par Spot 1043 GMT     132.20 \par 3 Day Trend       Bullish \par Weekly Trend      Range \par 200 day ma        123.70 \par 3rd Resistance    133.82 \par 2nd Resistance    132.74 \par 1st Resistance    132.34 \par Pivot*            131.38 \par 1st Support       131.90 \par 2nd Support       131.50 \par 3rd Support       131.20 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Chiara Albanese at chiara.albanese@wsj.com [ 08-23-13 0743ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1033 1034 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4162 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020130823e98n0001l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
