\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Sharply Stronger on  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jeff Fick and Matthew Cowley   \par \uc2 909 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2013\par 21:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real closed sharply stronger against the U.S. dollar Friday as a $60 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program unveiled by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  provided some necessary relief to the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's program is aimed at providing companies and investors with the certainty they will be able to buy dollars if needed. It continues the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps taken by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days and weeks to try to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but adds more visibility and predictability.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is providing much-needed clarity to Brazilian markets, which we didn't have for a long time," said \uc2 Ilan Solot\uc2 , an analyst at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in London. "As far as stopping the bleeding, it does a really good job."\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained 3.3% to exit active trading at BRL2.3534 per U.S. dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. That was stronger than Thursday's closing price at BRL2.4406, before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced its new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program.\par \par \uc2 Late Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would provide at least $60 billion more in dollar liquidity through the end of the year. Under the plan, the bank will offer $3 billion of dollar loans and swaps per week in daily auctions starting Friday through Dec. 31.\par \par \uc2 The program, however, could be extended beyond the end of 2013, if needed, according to Tulio Maciel, head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economics department. Mr. Maciel said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  planned to do what was needed to "supply liquidity and assure hedge" for the normal functioning of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 In the first of the regularly scheduled auctions of dollar-credit lines held Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreed to buy an undisclosed volume of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Jan. 2 at an exchange rate of BRL2.4651 per dollar. The bank had offered to sell up to $1 billion at the auction. Similar dollar-credit line sales will be held every Friday through the end of the year. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also will hold its first swap auction under the new strategy on Monday, when swaps worth the equivalent of $500 million will be offered.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move was welcomed for providing more visibility to its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , replacing what have so far been unpredictable daily auctions. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already sold some $45 billion in dollar swap contracts so far this year. Unlike other central banks around the world, the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't have a direct impact on the country's $375 billion of foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 The strategy is seen as continuing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of trying to restrain wild swings in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rather than halting it in its tracks. Yet the plan underscores how much the financial world has changed since the U.S. Federal Reserve said it was contemplating an end to the easy-money policies adopted to cope with the financial and economic crisis that began in 2008.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian officials in recent years have struggled with an overvalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not a falling one. Finance Minister Guido Mantega became known for complaining he was the victim of a "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war" as Brazil's real gained against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 That has now turned sharply. The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened around 16% against the dollar so far this year, and about 2% so far this week. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had touched BRL1.55 per dollar in mid-2011.\par \par \uc2 "Ultimately, markets always end up taking a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  where they want it to go," said Chris Gaffney, senior market strategist at \uc2 EverBank Financial Corp\uc2 . (EVER). EverBank trades about $100 million across about 20 different \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  per day, while also holding about $1 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits.\par \par \uc2 Most of the current market movements, especially where emerging markets are concerned, are being driven by bets that the Fed will start reducing its bond purchases by $15 billion as early as September, Mr. Gaffney said. While he thinks a Fed move in September is unlikely, the announcement will have an immediate, negative impact for emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mr. Gaffney added.\par \par \uc2 "I think the beginning of the taper will be the shock," with markets then likely to take a step back to evaluate how long before the cheap cash runs out, Mr. Gaffney said. EverBank is holding its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions steady until after the Fed's September meeting, with a plan to adjust positions afterward.\par \par \uc2 While much of the turn in market sentiment has been blamed on the Fed, the problems have been compounded by sluggish growth and high inflation in Brazil. Critics blame missteps in economic policy, including too much public spending, and say the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to weaken unless that changes.\par \par \uc2 But Mr. Gaffney said that he still owns the real, adding that expectations for higher interest rates to fight inflation and upcoming events such as next year's soccer World Cup and 2016 Summer Olympics could eventually boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "If [the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] can get in front of inflation, some of the hot money may move back into Brazil," Mr. Gaffney said.\par \par \uc2 --Gerald Jeffis in Brasilia contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 -Write to Jeff Fick at Jeff.Fick@wsj.com and Matt Cowley at matt.cowley@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 23, 2013 15:32 ET (19:32 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130823e98n0057a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
