\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  to Hold Regular  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Auctions to Offer Hedge\b0\par\par\uc2 184 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2013\par 00:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--\uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold regularly scheduled auctions of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and credit line repurchases in order to offer hedge and liquidity to the local market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The bank said it will hold regular auctions beginning Friday and extending through Dec. 31.\par \par \uc2 The institution said it would schedule daily swap auctions of up to $500 million on Monday through Thursday of each week and dollar repurchase auctions of up to $1 billion every Friday.\par \par \uc2 The bank said it would also take additional actions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market "if necessary."\par \par \uc2 Brazil has been holding frequent unscheduled swap and repurchase auctions over recent months in an effort to curb unusually heavy volatility in the exchange market prompted by repositioning of emerging market investors in anticipation of possible changes in U.S. monetary policy.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  last held regularly scheduled market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2002 amid investor uncertainties ahead of local elections during that year.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -0- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 08-22-13 1834ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020130822e98m0004p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
