\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil cenbank to sell dollars on spot market as  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  nears 5-year low\b0\par\par\uc2 157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2013\par 22:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Aug 21 (Reuters) - \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered on Wednesday to sell dollars on the spot market through repurchase agreements, in a bid to ease a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selloff that has driven the real to its weakest level in nearly five years.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement that on Thursday it will offer as much as $4 billion with repurchase dates set to Nov. 1 and April 1. It is the second time this week that the bank has resorted to this type of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The announcement was made after the bank conducted a survey to gauge market demand for dollar lines, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real plunged 2.3 percent on Thursday to close at 2.4501 per dollar, its weakest level since December 2008. (Reporting by Walter Brandimarte)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL\b0 \highlight\uc2 -REAL/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT) | ABN | D | M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130824e98l0009s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
