\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Brazil's Real Ends Six-Session Losing Streak\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 574 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 2013\par 22:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO--Brazil's besieged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended a string of six straight losing sessions against the dollar Tuesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 --and speculative investors paused to mull a series of sharp warnings from local authorities.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.3964 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, compared with its previous close of BRL2.4136. Monday saw the real settle at its weakest level in more than four years.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which until recently was considered overvalued by local exporters and industries, has seen far heavier losses than its counterparts in recent months, which threatens to fuel already-high inflation. The dollar has gained nearly 18% against the real in the past three months while advancing only 4.1% against the euro and 5.6% against the regional neighbor Mexican peso.\par \par \uc2 The real's decline had begun to steepen in the past few sessions, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening to current levels from BRL2.2703 on Aug. 11. But a round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by local authorities, combined with a growing view among market participants that the real had gone too far, helped to stop the bleeding Tuesday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the real three times Tuesday, holding two auctions of dollar-swap contracts and another auction of up to $4 billion in dollar credit lines. The former instrument helps investors hedge against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations via the futures market, while the latter offers cash dollars that must be returned to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a later date.\par \par \uc2 In addition to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly, Finance Minister Guido Mantega and \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Alexandre Tombini have both hinted this week that more forceful measures could be taken.\par \par \uc2 In a special statement posted on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's website Monday, Mr. Tombini "reminded" market participants that "the concentration of positions in a single direction can bring losses to those that bet on one-directional movements of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Mantega, for his part, said in an interview Tuesday with the local Estado news agency that he's not worried about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , adding that authorities have sufficient tools at their disposal to deal with volatility.\par \par \uc2 "It's good to heed the warnings that, instead of making money, one can lose," Mr. Mantega said. "Just like the dollar goes up, it can go down. Whoever thinks they're just going to win can lose money in this game."\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has yet to draw from its nearly $374 billion in international reserves to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a move that has market participants divided as to its potential for success. Some say it could be perceived as a sign of vulnerability and launch an even greater speculative attack on the real.\par \par \uc2 Luiz Carlos Baldan, director of Sao Paulo's Fourtrade brokerage, disputed the strength of local authorities' verbal warning to the market as well as Mr. Mantega's claim that the situation is "under control."\par \par \uc2 "At this rate, a lot of people's forecast of BRL2.70 will come true very soon, and if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  finally decides to auction dollars at that point, it will be too late," Mr. Baldan said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paul Kiernan at paul.kiernan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -Paulo Winterstein in Sao Paulo contributed to this report.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 20, 2013 16:23 ET (20:23 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130820e98k00595\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
