\par\par \b \uc2 Real halts 6-day slide as  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  steps up  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 2013\par 16:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Aug 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real gained for the first time in seven sessions on Tuesday after policymakers raised their rhetoric against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The real opened higher following overnight comments by Finance Minister Guido Mantega and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2 , both of whom advised investors to avoid strong bets against the real.\par \par \uc2 Their comments, which came on Monday after the real closed at its weakest level since March 2009, suggested they believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had overshot as it plummeted nearly 6 percent during six straight sessions of losses.\par \par \uc2 Most emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have sold off over the past few days as investors prepare for an expected withdrawal of U.S. stimulus measures. The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been specially hard-hit, however, as the country's slow-growing economy has fallen out of favor with investors.\par \par \uc2 After gaining more than 1 percent in the first hour of trading, the real shed some of its gains to rise a more modest 0.5 percent, at 2.4029 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Also supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were two auctions of traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, derivatives that emulate an injection of dollars in the futures market, and a third auction of spot dollars through repurchase agreements.\par \par \uc2 "The real is gaining because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is providing liquidity to both the spot and the futures market," said Sidnei Nehme, director at NGO brokerage in Sao Paulo. "By \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both markets, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is breaking the leg of speculators."\par \par \uc2 In the first swap auction, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 20,000 new contracts maturing on Jan 2. The second auction is designed to simply roll-over expiring maturities.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling swaps in the futures market to provide investors with protection against a further depreciation of the real. They are part of a government strategy to ease demand for dollars without burning the country's $370 billion in foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 Still, many analysts say that strategy has run its course as companies are unwilling to hedge again \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk at current exchange rate levels. Instead, they say, demand is growing for dollars on the spot market.\par \par \uc2 In an attempt to satisfy that demand without depleting its reserves, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also selling up to $4 billion in spot dollars on Tuesday with repurchase dates set to Jan. 2 and April 1. It is the first time in two months that policymakers resort to this type of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL\b0 \highlight\uc2 -REAL/ | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RBN | NAT | ABX | BNX | FUN | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130820e98k000mt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
