\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  rebound as U.S. yields fall\b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2013\par 00:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Aug 20 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  halted a prolonged selloff on Tuesday as \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  debt yields dropped for the first time in more than a week, bringing at least temporary relief to investors worried about an expected withdrawal of U.S. stimulus measures.\par \par \uc2 Major regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the Mexican peso and the Brazilian real , posted gains for the first time in at least seven sessions as U.S. benchmark 10-year Treasury note yields dropped to 2.82 percent from Monday's close of 2.88 percent.\par \par \uc2 Investors had been dumping emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past few days as expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve will cut back on its bond-buying program have sent Treasury yields soaring to two-year highs, reducing the allure of higher-yielding assets globally.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said, however, that Tuesday's recovery could prove to be temporary as investor jitters are not going away anytime soon.\par \par \uc2 Crucial for investors' expectations about the future of U.S. stimulus measures will be the release on Wednesday of minutes of the Fed's latest monetary policy meeting.\par \par \uc2 * The Brazilian real ended 0.9 percent stronger after slumping some 6 percent over six consecutive sessions of losses. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also supported by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid policymakers' heightened rhetoric against speculators.\par \par \uc2 * In a strategy to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both the futures and spot markets, selling traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and spot dollars through repurchase agreements.\par \par \uc2 * The Mexican peso rose 0.7 percent after seven straight sessions of losses, even as data showing an unexpected economic contraction in the second quarter disappointed economists.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  | ABN | D | M | RBN | NAT | C | E | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130823e98k0010u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
