\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Slides To New Low\b0\par\par\uc2 805 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 2013\par 01:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par C4\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (FROM THE WALL STREET JOURNAL 8/20/13) \par    By Erin McCarthy \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit a new low against the dollar amid increasing concerns that the country's policy makers are failing to reinvigorate the South American economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The real weakened to 2.4098 to the dollar on Monday, trading above 2.4 for the first time since March 2009. The decline came on the same day the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held a series of auctions that injected $3.6 billion into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, in an attempt to bolster the real.\par \par \uc2 Latin America's largest economy is grappling with sluggish growth and high inflation, a combination that has left policy makers in a bind and Brazilian assets, including its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , under pressure. The pace of the real's slide accelerated in late May, when U.S. Federal Reserve officials began to signal that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was prepared to wind down its bond-buying program later in the year.\par \par \uc2 Investors anticipating higher interest rates in the U.S. began pulling money out of emerging markets, with already struggling economies such as Brazil hit hardest. Funds that buy Brazilian bonds have seen $918 million in outflows since late May, according to data provider EPFR Global.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tried to fight the outflows by raising interest rates three times this year, raising the yields on the country's debt. It also has stepped up market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pumping $7.6 billion into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -futures market in the past week and $45.8 billion since May 31. The real is down more than 10% over that period.\par \par \uc2 "They're \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  like crazy, and it's still not working," said Sara Zervos, portfolio manager of the $11.7 billion Oppenheimer International Bond fund. "It's gotten to the point where investors and even domestic citizens have lost confidence in the ability of the government to navigate the country into growth."\par \par \uc2 Her firm has been steadily cutting its holdings of the Brazilian real and real-denominated Brazilian government bonds.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to offer liquidity to the market as needed, Alexandre Tombini, the bank's president, said Monday. Mr. Tombini also warned against betting too much on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves in one direction.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the real's slide is unlikely to reverse until the economic outlook improves. Forecasters expect economic growth of 2.2% in 2013, according to a \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey. That is up from last year but a far cry from the 7.5% growth in 2010. Meanwhile, inflation ran at 6.3% in July, near the top end of the government's target range. Brazil also swung to a $5 billion trade deficit through July, after a $9.9 billion surplus a year ago.\par \par \uc2 Barclays\uc2  on Friday predicted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hit 2.45 to the dollar in 12 months, from an earlier forecast of 2.20.\par \par \uc2 To be sure, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevent dangerous levels of volatility, and a number of investors agree that there might otherwise have been even steeper falls in the real.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is absolutely essential for controlling volatility," said Joao Paulo de Gracia Correa, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at brokerage Correparti. He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could have fallen as low as 2.7 per dollar in the past two weeks without the \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions.\par \par \uc2 And since its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are in the futures market, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't drawing on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. Other emerging markets, including Turkey, have seen their influence weakened in the market as they spent reserves.\par \par \uc2 Some investors also are willing to put up with a sliding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take advantage of Brazil's 8.5% benchmark interest rate, one of the world's highest.\par \par \uc2 Peter Wilson, co-manager of Wells Fargo Advantage International Bond Fund, holds real-denominated debt, and recently exited from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bets aimed at protecting against a drop in the real. He said he expects Brazil's economic problems to prove short-lived. "Over the longer term, we quite like" Brazil's bonds and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said.\par \par \uc2 Still, others worry that the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are a half-step -- too small to support the real, but large enough to drive off investors by introducing uncertainty about policy makers' next move.\par \par \uc2 "When you do this enough in small sizes, it becomes counterproductive," said James Barrineau, a portfolio manager on the Schroder Emerging Markets Multi-Sector Bond Fund at \uc2 Schroders PLC\uc2 , which has $357.5 billion under management. He said the real could weaken beyond 2.5 per dollar "if policy makers sit on their hands."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Barrineau owns Brazilian government bonds, but last week started buying contracts that protect those holdings should the real decline further.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 19, 2013 19:41 ET (23:41 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130819e98j0069v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
