\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real eases to 4-year low, Mexico peso flat\b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2013\par 22:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Aug 14 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real on Wednesday dropped to levels not seen in more than four years as investors tested policymakers' tolerance to a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the Mexican peso steadied after three consecutive sessions of losses. Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were generally calmer as comments by a senior U.S. Federal Reserve official were interpreted as supporting the continuity of the Fed's bond-buying program, maintaining investors' appetite for emerging market assets. St. Louis Fed president \uc2 James Bullard\uc2  said he has been concerned by U.S. low inflation, which does not seem to be heading higher despite the bank's stimulus measures. * The Brazilian real closed at 2.3240 per greenback, its weakest level since the end of March, 2009, leaving investors on watch for a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has routinely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market with the sale of traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, derivative contracts designed to support the real.\par \par \uc2  It has allowed the real to weaken about 1 percent on Tuesday, however, and another 0.6 percent on Wednesday. * "The market is testing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to see if it has abandoned the ship and will allow the real to weaken further," said a trader with a foreign bank in Brazil. * The Mexican peso steadied around 12.73 per dollar after losing about 1 percent during the past three sessions as investors assessed the likely impact of a proposed energy reform over future dollar inflows to the country. * \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  considered Mexico's reform proposal positive for the economy but cautioned that tangible benefits will only be seen in the long term. "This is because the reform requires a constitutional amendment and subsequent implementing regulation before contracts can be signed, and the related private investment can begin to flow," the ratings agency said in a statement. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prices at 1930 GMT:\par     \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                            Daily  YTD pct\par                                         pct   change\par                             Latest   change  \par  Brazil real                2.3240    -0.63   -12.22\par                                              \par  Mexico peso               12.7335     0.05     1.03\par                                              \par  Chile peso               508.0000     0.45    -5.77\par                                              \par  Colombia peso           1890.1000    -0.41    -6.57\par                                              \par  Peru sol                   2.7960    -0.04    -8.76\par                                              \par  Argentina peso             5.5650    -0.04   -11.73\par  Argentina peso             8.9000    -1.24   -23.82\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  | ABN | D | M | RBN | NAT | C | E | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130817e98e0009f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
