\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  weaken on Fed anxiety\b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2013\par 20:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Aug 12 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on Monday as investors were cautious before a series of U.S. economic data this week that could show the economy is gaining enough strength to survive with less monetary stimulus. The data, including Tuesday's retail sales reading, will be crucial for investors to determine whether the U.S. Federal Reserve may scale back, perhaps as early as next month, a bond-buying program that has fueled appetite for risk assets in emerging markets. * The Mexican peso rose as much as 0.55 percent early in the session as President Enrique Pena Nieto proposed a sweeping energy reform that could attract sizable foreign investment in the country, but later erased its gains. * The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  later traded 0.5 percent weaker at 12.6840 per dollar, in line with its Latin American peers. * The Brazilian real dropped 0.5 percent to 2.2830 per greenback, leaving investors on watch for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week sold traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, its instrument of choice for propping up the real, even when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was already strengthening against the dollar. "Considering the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I believe it is trying to prop up the real to fight inflation," said Jaime Ferreira, manager of the \b \highlight22\uc2 