\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Strengthens on  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2013\par 21:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real strengthened Thursday after an unexpected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.2830 to the dollar, stronger against the Wednesday close of BRL2.3086, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 The real strengthened slightly against the dollar in early trading as global investor sentiment improved. Investors were cheered by Chinese trade data showing a rise in imports by the Asian giant. Increased China demand brought a rise in global commodities prices. Brazil, in particular, benefits from greater Chinese demand since the Latin American country is a major exporter of farm commodities and mineral ores.\par \par \uc2 Early in the session, most traders had downplayed chances for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, noting that the bank rarely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is strengthening.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, at noon local time, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered up to $1 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts at auction. The market bought $631 million in the contracts.\par \par \uc2 The auctions offers investors the opportunity to exchange bonds linked to domestic interest rates for paper indexed directly to the U.S. dollar. The auctions typically strengthen the real by giving investors greater opportunities to hedge in the American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It [the auction] was a bit unexpected," said Mauricio Gaioti, a trader at Sao Paulo's Ouro Minas brokerage. "It shows that the government is very, very interested in pulling down inflation."\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real has depreciated about 11% against the U.S. dollar so far this year, contributing to Brazilian inflation. The weak real makes imports more expensive, including key products such as fuels, wheat and components for everything from mobile phones to motor vehicles.\par \par \uc2 Inflation is currently running at 6.3%.\par \par \uc2 "Bringing down inflation is still the government's top priority," said Mr. Gaioti. However, he noted, such factors as increased risk perception by foreign investors could mean more U.S. dollar outflows from Brazil. "There is still a market trend toward weakening of the real," he said, predicting more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming weeks as the government fights down inflation.\par \par \uc2 Write to Tom Murphy at tom.murphy@dowjones.com [ 08-08-13 1928GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130808e988000vq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
