\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Stronger After Another  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Luciana Magalhaes   \par \uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2013\par 22:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real closed stronger against the dollar on Friday after an initial drop, following yet another \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading Friday at BRL2.2779 to the dollar, after having touched BRL2.3118 to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the session, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. On Thursday, the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at BRL2.3008 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold another $1.75 billion in dollar-swap contracts Friday. The entire week was marked by heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has recently accelerated losses against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 On Friday some large \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  by few investors helped drive the dollar initially up, said Vanderlei Muniz, a trader at Brazilian brokerage Onnix.\par \par \uc2 "I expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be around BRL2.25 to BRL2.30 to the dollar in the next sessions," Mr. Muniz said. "It won't go beyond that because the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not allow it," he added.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the dollar also shed gains against major international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday after it was reported that the U.S. created fewer jobs than expected in July, spurring more doubts about when the Federal Reserve will decide to slow asset purchases.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is watching developments in the local jobs market as it considers its next steps for bond purchases. If companies continue to hire and unemployment falls as the Fed expects, it may start to wind down the program later this year.\par \par \uc2 Write to Luciana Magalhaes at luciana.magalhaes@dowjones.com [ 02-08-13 2021GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130802e982000u5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
