\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Changes Direction To Weaken Intraday\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 194 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2013\par 15:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA -- Brazil's real reversed its early strengthening trend to weaken in intraday action Thursday as investors bought up dollars amid thin liquidity.\par \par \uc2 As of 9:45 EDT, the real traded at BRL2.2861 according to Tullet Prebon via FactSet after ending at BRL2.2765 Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the market was reacting to strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar got cheap and the market went back to buying," said Reginaldo Galhardo, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at the Treviso brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  strongly in the market Wednesday, selling some $2.25 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps at three separate auctions to help curb the strength of the dollar as it approached BRL2.30.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -swap contracts allow investors to exchange bonds indexed to domestic interest rates for paper tied directly to the U.S. dollar. Typically, the swap auctions lead to a weakening of the U.S. dollar and a strengthening of the Brazilian real.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 01-08-13 1354GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130801e981000rs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
