\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes at Four-Year Low Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 645 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2013\par 00:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swung sharply Wednesday, ending the session at its weakest level against the dollar in more than four years, amid aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although in a late-afternoon twist, it was U.S. monetary policy that ultimately set the tone.\par \par \uc2 In an unusually lively day of action, \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $2.25 billion in dollar-futures contracts, a move investors have said is designed to arrest some of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's depreciation. Brazil is once again caught in the global spotlight, struggling to avoid stagflation while the U.S. economy shows signs of a faster recovery than had once been expected.\par \par \uc2 "We think Brazil needs a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," says \uc2 Marc Chandler\uc2 , global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at New York-based \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 , adding that he sees the real headed for BRL2.40. "We suspect the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is really meant to smooth it out rather than reverse it."\par \par \uc2 With the U.S. Federal Reserve expected to begin removing some of its easy-money policies in coming months, Mr. Chandler said, emerging markets are losing their allure.\par \par \uc2 The monetary stimulus, which began during the 2008 financial crisis, left world financial markets flush with liquidity that often headed for emerging markets such as Brazil. Yet signs of stronger growth in the U.S. have fed expectations that the Federal Reserve may begin to cut back on its $85 billion in monthly asset purchases.\par \par \uc2 The outlook for the U.S. economy contrasts sharply with Brazil, where forecasts for growth this year have been slashed to around 2.3%, from around 4% at the beginning of the year. The once-dynamic South American economy, which expanded 7.5% in 2010, could be headed for a fourth straight year of growth below 4% if current expectations for this year and next play out.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has expressed concern that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness may hamper its efforts to curtail inflation, which is running at around 6.7% per year, well above authorities' 4.5% target.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held three auctions to sell swap contracts, which give buyers an opportunity to protect themselves against abrupt \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations and tend to prop up the real against the dollar. It sold $2.25 billion in total in the first two auctions, but decided not to accept any bids in the third auction. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to try to prevent too much volatility.\par \par \uc2 The move, however, was seen as particularly surprising given that the market was engaged in month-end jostling to set the exchange rate for settling futures contracts that expire Thursday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has in the past avoided \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on these settlement days, preferring to let the market set the tone.\par \par \uc2 "I think we're going to continue seeing quite a lot of pressure on the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which will also feed inflation," says Joao Medeiros, a partner at Pioneer Corretora de Cambio Ltda. in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's auctions had some temporary effect on the real, sending it stronger against the dollar, although ultimately the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to weaken, pushing up close to BRL2.2300.\par \par \uc2 Yet, in a final twist, the Federal Reserve on Wednesday confounded some of the expectations about U.S. economic growth. The policy-setting Federal Open Market Committee, in its statement, suggest growth was "modest" rather than "moderate." Investors immediately pushed back their expectations for when the stimulus would come to an end, and plowed money back into emerging markets. The real recovered most of the day's losses, ending at BRL2.2765 a dollar, compared with BRL2.2727 at Tuesday's close.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paul Kiernan at paul.kiernan@wsj.com [ 31-07-13 2258GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130731e97v0016w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
