\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Calls Second Dollar Swap Auction\b0\par\par\uc2 373 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 2013\par 15:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 This was corrected at 10:02 a.m. EDT because the original misstated the information. [ 31-07-13 1358GMT ]\par \par \uc2 By \uc2 Matthew Cowley\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered some of its early-morning losses against the dollar after unusually aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in a highly volatile session.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  held three lightning dollar swap auctions Wednesday, as it sought to arrest the rapid depreciation of the real against the U.S. dollar. The exchange rate had slumped sharply ahead of data releases in the U.S., approaching BRL2.2300 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 At that point, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped, and sold $1.491 billion in dollar swap contracts due Jan. 2 in the first auction and $757.5 million due Feb. 3 in the second auction. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't accept any bids for the third auction.\par \par \uc2 These steps were separate from the auctions held in recent days, in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rolled over $5.7 billion in contracts that are due to expire on Aug. 1.\par \par \uc2 The swap contracts offer investors the opportunity to exchange bonds linked to domestic interest rates for paper indexed directly to the U.S. dollar. They effectively offer investors a hedge against abrupt \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations and typically help support the Brazilian real against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were unusual given that monthly futures contracts expire Thursday. They will close out based on Wednesday's average \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, known as the Ptax rate. The futures expiry often brings volatile trading as banks and investment funds jockey to influence the Ptax rate.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has in the past avoided stepping into the market on such days, although it did so at the end of June.\par \par \uc2 The real recovered some of its losses against the dollar, although it lost ground again after the result of the third auction was announced. by 11:09 ET, the real was trading at BRL2.2846 to-the-dollar, having earlier touched BRL2.2992, the weakest level since March 2009. The real ended Tuesday at BRL2.2779.\par \par \uc2 Write to \uc2 Matthew Cowley\uc2  at matthew.cowley@wsj.com [ 31-07-13 1517GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130731e97v000zx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
