\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  calls 3rd swap auction to halt  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  slide\b0\par\par\uc2 160 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 2013\par 16:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, July 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for a third time on Wednesday, in an attempt to halt a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slide that has driven the real to an over four-year low.\par \par \uc2 The bank said in a statement it will auction as many as 15,000 traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps maturing on March 2, 2014. It earlier sold 30,000 swaps expiring on Jan. 2, 2014 and 15,300 contracts maturing on March 2, 2014.\par \par \uc2 Traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps are derivative contracts designed to support the real.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at 2.2826 per U.S. dollar after the announcement of the third swap auction, 0.15 percent weaker for the day, after sliding as low as 2.3022, its weakest since April 1, 2009.\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-REAL/THIRDSWAP (URGENT) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | U | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130731e97v000u9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
