\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  ends flat as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  acts, Fed fears ease\b0\par\par\uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 2013\par 14:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  3 times to support real\par \par \uc2 * Fed offers no hint of imminent stimulus tapering\par \par \uc2 * Real falls to lowest in over 4 years but then erases losses\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte and Bruno Federowski\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, July 31 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended little changed on Wednesday after heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a U.S. Federal Reserve decision to continue its bond-buying program propped up the real after it fell to the lowest in more than 4 years.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times in the market during the morning as it fought to stop the real from weakening past the psychologically relevant mark of 2.3 per dollar - avoiding an additional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation that could add to inflation.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  came right after the real slumped to as much as 2.3022 per dollar, its weakest level since April 1, 2009. The slide was magnified by investors trying to influence an official month-end exchange rate known as PTAX, which is reference for a broad range of contracts including foreign loans.\par \par \uc2 At the end of the day, the real closed 0.08 percent weaker at 2.2809 per greenback.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to keep the exchange rate between 2.2 and 2.3 per dollar in order to avoid a very undesirable inflation pressure in the next few months," said Eduardo Velho, chief economist at INVX Global brokerage in Sao Paulo. "It looks like the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will fight hard to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at that level. The question is whether it will succeed. I believe it can win in the short term."\par \par \uc2 In two separate auctions, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a total of 45,300 traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, derivative contracts that emulate an injection of dollars in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 However, it found no demand for the swaps offered at a third auction, leading some analysts to conclude that the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  served to provide enough liquidity to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for now.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been forced to provide dollar liquidity as investors anticipate a slowdown in the pace of U.S. bond purchases by the Fed. Part of the dollars the Fed has injected in the U.S. economy has been flowing to emerging markets during the past few years.\par \par \uc2 Speculation that the Fed would hint at reducing its stimulus program increased after data showed the U.S. economy unexpectedly accelerated in the second quarter.\par \par \uc2 The data showed U.S. gross domestic product expanded at a 1.7 percent annual rate in the second quarter, above the 1 percent rate forecast by economists and up from the first quarter's downwardly revised 1.1 percent expansion pace.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. economic picture was also brightened by a report showing the U.S. private sector added 20,000 jobs in July.\par \par \uc2 But at the end of its two-day meeting, the Fed said the economy is still in need of support and that it will keep buying $85 billion in mortgage and Treasury securities per month.\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-REAL/DROPS (UPDATE 2) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | C | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130731e97v000p1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
