\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Weaker Early on Following Jobs Data\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2013\par 15:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--Brazil's real weakened in early trading Wednesday as investors pondered the latest signs that Brazil's labor market could be cooling.\par \par \uc2 As of 9:15 a.m. EDT, the real was trading at BRL2.2274 to the dollar after ending at BRL2.2210 to the dollar Tuesday, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's IBGE statistics institute Tuesday reported unemployment in the country rose slightly in June, moving to 6% in the month from 5.8% in May. Employment also showed its first year-on-year decline since 2009.\par \par \uc2 Analysts noted the Brazilian jobs data could prompt caution from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in extending its recent interest rate tightening cycle. The bank has raised its benchmark Selic rate in recent months to 8.5% from an all-time low of 7.25% at the beginning of the year.\par \par \uc2 The real was also seeing influence Wednesday from discouraging economic data in China, where the purchasing managers' index fell to 47.7 in July from 48.8 in June. That offset better news from Europe, where the PMI rose in the month to 50.4 in July from 48.7 previously.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, meanwhile, was also on the lookout for signals that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in coming days with more dollar swap auctions. The bank is seen possibly rolling over $5.7 billion in swap contracts coming due on Aug. 1 and another $5 billion on Sept. 2.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept a regular presence in the local market over recent months to curb the weakenening of the real, which has slipped about 8% against the dollar amid signs the U.S. Federal Reserve may be preparing to tighten monetary policy in coming quarters and attract investor dollar away from key emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 24-07-13 1331GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130724e97o000jg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
