\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Stocks Rise,  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Weakens After U.S. Fed Minutes\b0\par\par\uc2 By Matthew Cowley   \par \uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2013\par 22:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--Brazilian stocks rose on Wednesday, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened against the dollar, as investors digested the minutes from the latest U.S. Federal Open Market Committee meeting.\par \par \uc2 The minutes showed Fed officials divided about the timing of a reduction in bond buying, with half of the Fed officials believing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should end the stimulus program by the end of this year. That disappointed traders hoping for a clearer timetable, and sent the dollar lower against its rivals.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the release of the minutes to contain some of the earlier depreciation of the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the equivalent of $1.48 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts for two different dates, Dec. 2, 2013 and Jan. 2, 2014.\par \par \uc2 Typically, such auctions help support the real against the U.S. dollar by offering investors the opportunity to exchange bonds linked to domestic interest rates for paper indexed directly to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.2685 per dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had traded as weak as BRL2.2787 before the auction was called.\par \par \uc2 Stocks, meanwhile, saw a tepid rise, after the market had given back strong gains earlier in the session. \uc2 Vale SA\uc2 , one of the main blue chips, was up 1.4%, at BRL26.44; oil company \uc2 Petroleo Brasileiro SA\uc2 , or \uc2 Petrobras\uc2 , was up 1.5% at BRL15.21.\par \par \uc2 Oil company \uc2 OGX Petroleo e Gas Participacoes SA\uc2  ended 13.5% higher after EBX, the holding company of \uc2 Eike Batista\uc2 , announced it had restructured debts with Abu Dhabi's \uc2 Mubadala Development Corporation\uc2 . The announcement lacked any important details but analysts said the deal could give Mr. Batista extra time, perhaps by repaying Mubadala over a longer period along with lower interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Write to \uc2 Matthew Cowley\uc2  at matthew.cowley@dowjones.com \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @MattCowleyBR [ 10-07-13 2034GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1836 1843 5053 5076   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130710e97a000pb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
