\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Strengthens After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2013\par 21:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real strengthened Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to arrest an early trend toward depreciation against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.2571 to-the-dollar, stronger against the Wednesday close of BRL2.2655, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 The real weakend to BRL2.27 against the dollar Thursday morning. But the trend toward depreciation brought swift \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by calling an auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the equivalent of $1.26 billion in swaps. Such auctions typically serve to support the real by giving investors the opportunity to obtain bonds indexed directly to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reinforced its effort to hold the line against depreciation by announcing, at the end of trading Thursday, a swap auction for early Friday morning. The bank said it will sell up to $2 billion in swaps at the Friday morning auction.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not be able to hold the real at present values for the long term, however.\par \par \uc2 "Depreciation of the real against the dollar is a long-term trend," said Mauricio Gaioti, a trader at Sao Paulo's Ouro Minas brokerage. "Nor does it depend much on the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or even the Brazilian market. The dollar is gaining against all the emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The reason for the dollar's strength is the expectation that the U.S. Federal Reserve will soon wind down its policy of monetary loosening. The policy shift will lead to higher U.S. interest rates, draining investment dollars away from emerging markets and back to the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Write to Tom Murphy at tom.murphy@dowjones.com [ 04-07-13 1951GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130704e974000kn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
