\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Closes Stronger as Exporters Bring Dollars Home\b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2013\par 21:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real closed stronger against the dollar Monday as exporters took advantage of recent weakness of Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bring money home from the U.S.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.2266 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, after closing at BRL2.2406 on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The real had opened weaker against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , crossing the BRL2.26 line twice early in the session. Over the course of the day, the real gradually gained against the dollar to close stronger.\par \par \uc2 "There are always exporters with dollars out there waiting for a good time to bring their money back home," said Sidnei Nehme, director of the NGO brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The real should nevertheless tend to weaken against the dollar in coming days and weeks as signs the U.S. economy is steadily improving increase the likelihood of rising interest rates in the world's biggest economy, Mr. Nehme said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly last week to try to keep the real from weakening too quickly, and will probably continue to step in from time to time, according to Paulo Fujisaki, an analyst at the Socopa brokerage.\par \par \uc2 "There's a certain amount of inflation related to the stronger dollar," he said, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to fight against rising prices.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian economists and analysts increased their inflation view for the end of this year to 5.86% from 5.83%. For the end of 2014, economists and analysts maintained their view for inflation at 5.8%, according to a weekly \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey released Monday.\par \par \uc2 Write to \uc2 Jeffrey T. Lewis\uc2  at jeffrey.lewis@dowjones.com [ 24-06-13 1927GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130624e96o000oz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
