\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil currency \highlight\uc2  dives, rate futures soar despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 714 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2013\par 14:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Real tumbles to over 4-year low on Fed, China concerns\par \par \uc2 * Interest rate futures soar as weaker real seen fueling inflation\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, dollar sales on spot market\par \par \uc2 * Treasury repurchases local government debt to stabilize market\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte and Natalia Cacioli\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, June 20 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell sharply on Thursday and interest-rate futures soared for a second day, defying government efforts to stabilize both markets, as investors fret about a likely withdrawal of U.S. stimulus and an economic slowdown in China.\par \par \uc2 The real closed 1.6 percent lower at 2.2568 per dollar, its weakest level in more than four years, complicating government efforts to rein in inflation. Since the beginning of May, the real has lost more than 11 percent.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rout deepened a day after Federal Reserve Chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2  said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably reduce its stimulus program this year and finish it by mid-2014. The Fed's stimulus has kept U.S. interest rates low for years, supporting investor appetite for emerging-market assets.\par \par \uc2 Chinese factory activity slowed in June to a nine-month low, adding to worries about slower demand from the main market for some of Brazil's principal exports such as iron ore and soybeans.\par \par \uc2 "Markets are going through a panic moment. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , within its possibilities, is doing its job (to calm down investors) but the sentiment is pretty bad," said Glauber Romano, a trader at the Intercam brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Thursday, \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 30,000 traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts due on Sept. 2 and another 30,000 contracts maturing on Oct. 1, a strategy that emulates the sale of dollars in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 The contracts provide investors with a hedge, a kind of insurance, against further declines in the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  only briefly supported the real, however.\par \par \uc2 In early afternoon, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  returned to the market with an auction of as much as $3 billion directly on the spot market, in an attempt to provide temporary dollar liquidity to the system.\par \par \uc2 The bank said it intended to sell the greenbacks with repurchase agreement dates set for September 3 and October 1.\par \par \uc2 INTEREST-RATE FUTURES SOAR\par \par \uc2 The rout in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market contributed to pushing interest-rate futures sharply higher on the BM&FBovespa exchange.\par \par \uc2 Investors fear that the sharp depreciation of the real will further stoke inflation by increasing the price of imported goods, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to increase its benchmark Selic interest rate more aggressively.\par \par \uc2 The spike in interest-rate futures came in spite of news that Brazil's two biggest cities agreed to revoke an increase in public transportation fares following nationwide protests against poor public services.\par \par \uc2 Lower bus fares should reduce the benchmark IPCA inflation index by 0.1 percentage point, calculated Daniel Cunha, an economist with XP Investimentos in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The move seemed insufficient to ease concerns about the long-term inflation trends. Reports of heavy selling of domestic government bonds by foreigners also contributed to the increase in local interest rates, traders said.\par \par \uc2 In an attempt to stabilize the secondary market for domestic debt, the Brazilian Treasury conducted extraordinary auctions to repurchase government bonds for the second time this week, resorting to a strategy it had not used since 2008.\par \par \uc2 "After the Fed statement, we understand the market needs price parameters," said a Treasury official who asked not to be named. "That is the reason for those extraordinary auctions."\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the Treasury bought back a little over 1 million LTN and NTN-F notes, fixed-rate debt instruments regularly sold by the government. It had initially offered to repurchase as much 4 million of such notes.\par \par \uc2 It also bought back 240 million inflation-protected NTN-B notes, out of an initial repurchase offer of up to 2 million of those instruments.\par \par \uc2 Additional repurchase auctions of LTN, NTN-F and NTN-B will be held on Friday, the Finance Ministry said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL/REAL (UPDATE 3) | ABN | D | G | RBN | M | NAT | UKI | C | E | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD | PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130620e96k000oe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
