\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Brazil real dives 2 pct as Fed signals end to stimulus\b0\par\par\uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2013\par 20:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Fed likely to reduce stimulus this year, end it by mid-2014\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real slumps to weakest level since April 2009\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrains from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  slide\par \par \uc2 By Bruno Federowski\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, June 19 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped nearly 2 percent on Wednesday to close at a more than four-year low after U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2  suggested the bank's stimulus program, which has supported investors' appetite for emerging market assets, could end within the next 12 months.\par \par \uc2 The real closed at 2.2198 per dollar, its weakest since the end of April 2009 and down 1.9 percent for the day, as investors feared a reduction in U.S. stimulus measures would ease the flow of dollars seeking higher returns in emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had firmed slightly earlier in the session as exporters decided to take advantage of the real's recent slide to sell some dollars. But gains vanished in the afternoon after the Federal Reserve said in a statement that downside risks to the U.S. economic outlook had diminished since the fall.\par \par \uc2 The selloff gained traction after Bernanke said that, if economic forecasts are correct, policymakers will likely reduce the pace of bond purchases this year, before ending the program by the middle of next year.\par \par \uc2 "First, the Fed brought more positive (economic) forecasts and then Bernanke said the bank is nearing the moment to cut down on stimulus," said Luciano Rostagno, chief strategist at \uc2 WestLB\uc2  bank in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "I expected Bernanke to calm down investors who were worried about a reduction in the purchases (of bonds), but he indicated that those investors are on the right track."\par \par \uc2 After Wednesday's slump, the real has weakened about 9 percent since the beginning of May, when it was trading around 2 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Despite the sell-off, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, a sign that policymakers considered the real's depreciation in line with that of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In Mexico, the peso also slid more than 2 percent after Bernanke's comments.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL/REAL (UPDATE 2) | ABN | D | M | RBN | NAT | C | E | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130619e96j000zl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
