\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Tombini: Global Liquidity Won't Disappear Suddenly\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paulo Trevisani   \par \uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2013\par 21:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--The world will have high levels of liquidity for quite some time, but the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if volatility gets too intense, said \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In a regular testimony to senators, Mr. Tombini said that inflation "is and will remain under control."\par \par \uc2 The IPCA price index, closely monitored by the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has been around 6.5%, the top of the bank's targeted range. As a result, interest rates were upped to 8% in May, from 7.5%. New increases are expected.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tombini said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "is vigilant and will do what is needed in a timely fashion" to bring inflation down.\par \par \uc2 The bank has also been very active in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the past two weeks, as investors sold off Brazilian reais and other emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The trend was sparked by a perception that the U.S. Federal Reserve will reduce monetary stimulus in place since the aftermath of the 2008 financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tombini said the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are meant to "remove volatility when we think it is excessive," but that the policy is to let the real float. "We have a floating [\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] policy...to absorb positive shocks as well as negative ones," he said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paulo Trevisani at paulo.trevisani@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 This was corrected 0709 EDT June 18, 2013 to fix the \uc2 Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's previous base interest rate. Interest rates were raised to 8% in May from 7.5%, not from 7.25%. [ 06-18-13 1512ET ]\par \par \uc2 The story "Brazil's Tombini: Global Liquidity Won't Disappear Suddenly," published Tuesday at 3:12 p.m. EDT, misstated the \uc2 Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's previous base interest rate. Interest rates were raised to 8% in May from 7.5%, not from 7.25%. [ 06-19-13 0722ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020130618e96i0005e\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (brazil near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjus